---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";

const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL;
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Awesome GitHub"
  description="A compact GitHub-led site for planning, governance, and AI-assisted workflows."
>
  <section class="hero">
    <div class="eyebrow">Phase 1 MVP</div>
    <h1>Awesome GitHub</h1>
    <p class="lede">
      A compact GitHub-led website that explains how LightSpeed uses the `.github`
      repository as a practical control plane for planning, governance, and AI-assisted
      workflows.
    </p>
    <div class="hero-actions">
      <a class="button primary" href={`${base}why-this-exists/`}>Why this exists</a>
      <a class="button secondary" href={`${base}references/`}>Browse references</a>
    </div>
    <div class="kicker">What ships first</div>
    <div class="stat-list">
      <div class="stat">
        <strong>3 pages</strong>
        Home, why this exists, and references.
      </div>
      <div class="stat">
        <strong>Source-backed</strong>
        Copy normalised from the planning briefs and reference site.
      </div>
      <div class="stat">
        <strong>Phase-ready</strong>
        Designed so phase 2 can grow into a fuller resource catalogue.
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <h2>Browse the MVP</h2>
    <div class="card-grid">
      <article class="card">
        <h3>Home</h3>
        <p>Clear positioning, a short value statement, and direct paths into the rest of the site.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="card">
        <h3>Why this exists</h3>
        <p>A concise explanation of the repository-as-control-plane model and the reason for the site.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="card">
        <h3>References</h3>
        <p>Primary links to the source repo, the live reference site, and the planning inputs.</p>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <h2>Phase 2 direction</h2>
    <div class="page-copy">
      <p>
        The next phase will expand this into a fuller resource site with categories,
        browsing paths, and richer content models. Phase 1 keeps the surface area small
        so the site can be launched and iterated on quickly.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
